# model = zubko_BARE_GR_S
# Size-integrated extinction, albedo and scattering asymmetry per H
# for the Zubko, Dwek & Arendt (2004) BARE-GR-S dust model.
#
# Model definition: ZDA 2004, ApJS 152, 211, bare grains, PAH +
#   graphite + silicate; the files are the copies distributed with the
#   Camps et al. (2015) radiative-transfer benchmark.
# Optics (all three components): the DustEM/Zubko Q tables
#   ../data/zubko/PAH_28_1201_neu.dat, Gra_121_1201.dat, suvSil_121_1201.dat
#   These are the authors' own multilayer-sphere solution, so Q_sca and
#   <cos> are read from the same file as Q_abs rather than recomputed
#   from a dielectric function this model does not supply.
# Size distribution: the ZDA log-polynomial FORMULA evaluated on the
#   optics-table radii, with the coefficients read from
#   ../data/zubko/ZDA_BARE_GR_S_Config.dat
#
# Wavelength range:  1.000000E-03 -  1.000000E+04 um, 1201 points.
#   The range is the ZDA optics table itself, 1.24 keV down to 1.24e-4 eV.
#   This model has no EUV extension and needs none: its tabulated
#   optics already cover the whole ionizing band, and those tables ARE
#   the model definition, so there is no dielectric function to extend
#   them with.
#
# Column order follows Draine's kext_albedo tables and MoCHII's
#   par%ion_dust_kext reader: the first four columns are
#   lambda, albedo, <cos>, C_ext/H, and a reader may stop there.
#   Draine's 5th column is K_abs [cm^2/g]; ours is C_abs/H [cm^2/H],
#   so no dust-mass normalization is folded into the first six
#   columns; K_abs is a separate trailing column instead.
#   A host running the Zubko model through an ionizing band needs
#   exactly such a file: that model has no EUV extension of its own
#   (its optics table IS the model definition), so the host reads the
#   ionizing-band optics from a curve file instead.
#
# SCOPE: these are size-integrated TRANSPORT optics, not a dust model.
#   There is no size-resolved Cabs(lambda, a), no grain enthalpy and no
#   Planck integral here, so stochastic heating and thermal emission
#   cannot be computed from this file.  A host that needs emission must
#   build the model (build_astrodust / build_dl07 / build_zubko /
#   build_from_files).  The builder reads this very curve back in, and
#   dust_extinction serves it on the model wavelength grid while
#   dust_emission supplies the re-emitted spectrum, so the absorbed
#   power and the emission refer to one and the same grain.
#
# Units: lambda micron; cross sections cm^2 per H nucleon;
#   albedo and <cos> dimensionless.
#
# K_abs [cm^2/g] = C_abs/H / (M_dust/N_H), M_dust/N_H =  1.443932E-26 g/H.
#   The dust mass per H is this model's own size distribution
#   weighted by the solid density of each grain material:
#   M_dust/N_H = sum_pop rho * sum_a (4/3) pi a^3 dn(a).
#   Densities: the Density entry in the header of each component's own DustEM optics table.
#
#             lambda               albedo                <cos>              C_ext/H              C_abs/H              C_sca/H                K_abs
#           (micron)                                                       (cm^2/H)             (cm^2/H)             (cm^2/H)             (cm^2/g)
